 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "In a group of 100 people, 35 people wear glasses, 40 people wear contacts, 12 wear both glasses and contacts, and 25 wear neither glasses nor contacts.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 454452,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Are the events “person wears glasses” and “person wears contacts” mutually exclusive?\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "See Solution Manual\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "These events are not mutually exclusive since a person can use both glasses and contacts."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 454453,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Calculate the probability that a randomly chosen person wears glasses or contacts. Round your answer to 3 decimal places.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "Since we are asked to find the probability that a randomly chosen person wears glasses or contacts, use the probability formula:<br><span data-math=\"P\\left( {A\\;\\mathrm{or}\\;B} \\right) = P\\left( A \\right) + P\\left( B \\right) - P\\left( {A\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;B} \\right),\\;\\mathrm{when}\\;A,\\;B\\;\\mathrm{are}\\;\\mathrm{not}\\;\\mathrm{mutually}\\;\\mathrm{exclusive}\\;\\mathrm{events}\"></span><br><span data-math=\"P\\left( {\\mathrm{glasses}\\;\\mathrm{or}\\;\\mathrm{contacts}} \\right) = P\\left( {\\mathrm{glasses}} \\right) + P\\left( {\\mathrm{contacts}} \\right) - P\\left( {\\mathrm{glasses}\\;\\mathrm{and}\\;\\mathrm{contacts}} \\right)\"></span><br><span data-math=\"P\\left( {\\mathrm{glasses}\\;\\mathrm{or}\\;\\mathrm{contacts}} \\right) = \\frac{{35}}{{100}} + \\frac{{40}}{{100}} - \\frac{{12}}{{100}} = \\frac{{63}}{{100}} = 0.63\"></span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.63 "
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
